    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.tabline\n\n### Question\n\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/6a69dcf8-b8b2-41a3-b0dc-787fcb7f49e7)\r\nHi everyone ! I have an silly question. \r\nIt possible to hide the (*) button everytime start neovim?. It seems the (*) button is only available only if that buffer is empty. Like [No buffer]. ",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.tabline</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" href=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/179551485/403677943-6a69dcf8-b8b2-41a3-b0dc-787fcb7f49e7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTMyNDIsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1Mjk0MiwicGF0aCI6Ii8xNzk1NTE0ODUvNDAzNjc3OTQzLTZhNjlkY2Y4LWI4YjItNDFhMy1iMGRjLTc4N2ZjYjdmNDllNy5wbmc_.uNakuCR3ml1SdK_TanA44O9h95_R4pdmeq1dMZKAKxc\"><img src=\"https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/179551485/403677943-6a69dcf8-b8b2-41a3-b0dc-787fcb7f49e7.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9.eyJpc3MiOiJnaXRodWIuY29tIiwiYXVkIjoicmF3LmdpdGh1YnVzZXJjb250ZW50LmNvbSIsImtleSI6ImtleTUiLCJleHAiOjE3OTM1NTMyNDIsIm5iZiI6MTc5MzU1Mjk0MiwicGF0aCI6Ii8xNzk1NTE0ODUvNDAzNjc3OTQzLTZhNjlkY2Y4LWI4YjItNDFhMy1iMGRjLTc4N2ZjYjdmNDllNy5wbmc_.uNakuCR3ml1SdK_TanA44O9h95_R4pdmeq1dMZKAKxc\" alt=\"image\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"></a><br>\nHi everyone ! I have an silly question.<br>\nIt possible to hide the (<em>) button everytime start neovim?. It seems the (</em>) button is only available only if that buffer is empty. Like [No buffer].</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.tabline\nQuestion\n\nHi everyone ! I have an silly question.\nIt possible to hide the () button everytime start neovim?. It seems the () button is only available only if that buffer is empty. Like [No buffer].",
    "category": {
        "createdAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z",
        "description": "Ask the community for help",
        "emoji": ":pray:",
        "emojiHTML": "<div>🙏</div>",
        "id": "DIC_kwDOFoksYM4CAgqN",
        "isAnswerable": true,
        "name": "Q&A",
        "slug": "q-a",
        "updatedAt": "2022-01-02T14:24:09Z"
    },
    "closed": false,
    "closedAt": null,
    "comment_count": 1,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author": {
                "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62192487?u=a36947d53d29eebdd44445978c89853446d108f0&v=4",
                "login": "krovuxdev",
                "resourcePath": "/krovuxdev",
                "url": "https://github.com/krovuxdev"
            },
            "authorAssociation": "NONE",
            "body": "You can try the following solution. It ensures that empty and unnamed buffers (like the ones created by `:tabnew`) are not listed in the buffer list:\r\n```lua\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"BufAdd\", \"BufEnter\" }, {\r\n    callback = function(args)\r\n        if vim.bo[args.buf].buftype == \"\" and vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf) == \"\" then\r\n            vim.bo[args.buf].buflisted = false\r\n        end\r\n    end,\r\n})",
            "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">You can try the following solution. It ensures that empty and unnamed buffers (like the ones created by <code class=\"notranslate\">:tabnew</code>) are not listed in the buffer list:</p>\n<div class=\"highlight highlight-source-lua notranslate position-relative overflow-auto\" dir=\"auto\" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content=\"vim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ &quot;BufAdd&quot;, &quot;BufEnter&quot; }, {\n    callback = function(args)\n        if vim.bo[args.buf].buftype == &quot;&quot; and vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf) == &quot;&quot; then\n            vim.bo[args.buf].buflisted = false\n        end\n    end,\n})\"><pre class=\"notranslate\"><span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_create_autocmd</span>({ <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>BufAdd<span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span></span>, <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span>BufEnter<span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span>}, {\n    <span class=\"pl-en\">callback</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">function</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>)\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">if</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">buftype</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">and</span> <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">api</span>.<span class=\"pl-c1\">nvim_buf_get_name</span>(<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>) <span class=\"pl-k\">==</span> <span class=\"pl-s\"><span class=\"pl-pds\">\"</span><span class=\"pl-pds\">\" </span></span><span class=\"pl-k\">then</span>\n            <span class=\"pl-smi\">vim</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">bo</span>[<span class=\"pl-smi\">args</span>.<span class=\"pl-e\">buf</span>].<span class=\"pl-e\">buflisted</span> <span class=\"pl-k\">=</span> <span class=\"pl-c1\">false</span>\n        <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>\n    <span class=\"pl-k\">end</span>,\n})</pre></div>",
            "bodyText": "You can try the following solution. It ensures that empty and unnamed buffers (like the ones created by :tabnew) are not listed in the buffer list:\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ \"BufAdd\", \"BufEnter\" }, {\n    callback = function(args)\n        if vim.bo[args.buf].buftype == \"\" and vim.api.nvim_buf_get_name(args.buf) == \"\" then\n            vim.bo[args.buf].buflisted = false\n        end\n    end,\n})",
