                    "upvoteCount": 0,
                    "url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1485#discussioncomment-11850866"
                },
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "> It possible to hide the (_) button everytime start neovim?. It seems the (_) button is only available only if that buffer is empty. Like [No buffer].\r\n\r\nJust to clarify on [this solution](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/1485#discussioncomment-11850566). 'mini.tabline' shows [all listed buffers](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9e603a31d3fbc7ee61c9b556cd84e97fa2dcff53/doc/mini-tabline.txt#L8) (which basically means that they have 'buflisted' option set to `true` and thus are intended to be shown in (any) buffer list. It also has special symbols for unnamed buffers: `!` for scratch buffer and `*` for regular one. On the startup and after `:tabnew` there is one single listed regular unnamed buffer autocreated, thus the single `*` in tabline.\r\n\r\n> It seems i can't make `mini.icons` work with `mini.autocompletion`.\r\n\r\nYes, using either Neovim>=0.11 (current Nightly) or explicit `MiniIcons.tweak_lsp_kind()` is the way to go here.",
                    "bodyHTML": "<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It possible to hide the (<em>) button everytime start neovim?. It seems the (</em>) button is only available only if that buffer is empty. Like [No buffer].</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Just to clarify on <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/discussions/1485#discussioncomment-11850566\" data-hovercard-type=\"discussion\" data-hovercard-url=\"/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/1485/hovercard?comment_id=11850566\">this solution</a>. 'mini.tabline' shows <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/9e603a31d3fbc7ee61c9b556cd84e97fa2dcff53/doc/mini-tabline.txt#L8\">all listed buffers</a> (which basically means that they have 'buflisted' option set to <code class=\"notranslate\">true</code> and thus are intended to be shown in (any) buffer list. It also has special symbols for unnamed buffers: <code class=\"notranslate\">!</code> for scratch buffer and <code class=\"notranslate\">*</code> for regular one. On the startup and after <code class=\"notranslate\">:tabnew</code> there is one single listed regular unnamed buffer autocreated, thus the single <code class=\"notranslate\">*</code> in tabline.</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It seems i can't make <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.icons</code> work with <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.autocompletion</code>.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Yes, using either Neovim&gt;=0.11 (current Nightly) or explicit <code class=\"notranslate\">MiniIcons.tweak_lsp_kind()</code> is the way to go here.</p>",
                    "bodyText": "It possible to hide the () button everytime start neovim?. It seems the () button is only available only if that buffer is empty. Like [No buffer].\n\nJust to clarify on this solution. 'mini.tabline' shows all listed buffers (which basically means that they have 'buflisted' option set to true and thus are intended to be shown in (any) buffer list. It also has special symbols for unnamed buffers: ! for scratch buffer and * for regular one. On the startup and after :tabnew there is one single listed regular unnamed buffer autocreated, thus the single * in tabline.\n\nIt seems i can't make mini.icons work with mini.autocompletion.\n\nYes, using either Neovim>=0.11 (current Nightly) or explicit MiniIcons.tweak_lsp_kind() is the way to go here.",
